add('20e3d3',4.5,'Combinatorics',['strategy','parity'],'Preserve one odd pile and remaining ones, then handle the even-total endgame separately.',r'A move replaces two coprime positive integers on a board by their sum; a player unable to move loses. Prove the second player can win when the initial board contains (a) 2019 ones, (b) 2020 ones.')
add('321ef6',3.5,'Number theory',['integer triangles','factorization'],'The inradius identity and Pythagoras reduce to (a−8)(b−8)=32, followed by a short divisor check.')
add('469146',6.5,'Geometry',['nine-point circle','power of a point'],'Several orthic-triangle similarities locate the midpoint on a key circle; the angle inequality then locates N.',r'In acute $ABC$ with $AB>AC$, let $D,E,F$ be its altitude feet. Put $P=EF\cap BC$. The parallel to $EF$ through $D$ meets $AC,AB$ at $Q,R$. If $N\in BC$ satisfies $\angle NQP+\angle NRP<180^\circ$, prove $BN>CN$.')
