add('ec3990',5.5,'Algebra',['homogeneity','Cauchy-Schwarz','AM-GM'],'Normalize the sum, split the expression, then choose a weighted Cauchy bound controlled by a three-term AM-GM estimate.',r'For $a,b,c>0$, prove $\sum_{\mathrm{cyc}}\frac{\sqrt{a+b+c}+\sqrt a}{b+c}\ge\frac{9+3\sqrt3}{2\sqrt{a+b+c}}$.')
